  "query_preview": "..High pressure in the mid to upper levels will be the\nmain story over the coming week. As a result, look for mainly\nclear skies, high temperatures 5-10 degrees above normal and\ngenerally light daytime winds from the northeast to southeast at\n5-15 mph locally gusting to 20 mph. Only a few deviations from \nthe above scenario. The first, during the overnight periods with \nclear skies and a dry air mass in place, strong radiational \ncooling will produce drainage flow south of the Mogollon Rim. As a\nresult, look for locally gusty nighttime winds of 10-25 mph for \nlocations such as Sedona, Black Canyon City, Cordes Junction and \nCrown King. Second, indications are that some moisture will try to\nsneak back over portions of eastern Arizona on Tuesday in \nresponse to a weak shortwave trough brushing the state. We'll know\nmore as time draws nearer but for now it looks like it would be \nthe White Mountains that would see a slight chance of \nafternoon/evening showers and thunderstorms.",
